    fix(schema): invalidate declared-table registry on declaration changes
    
    Addresses REG-GONE-002. The in-process registryCache in
    src/schema/table-registry.ts never invalidated: an out-of-band rewrite of
    tables/table.table.json (e.g. the auger foreman's 13-table rewrite) stayed
    invisible to GET /api/ns/<ns>/tables until a daemon restart, and
    declare-extended columns were refused with 400 Unknown column(s).
    legacyDeclarations() now stats the tables dir per read and re-reads when
    the listing or any file's mtime/size changed (out-of-band writers), and the
    in-process declare path in src/serialization/ddl.ts now calls
    invalidateTableRegistry(ns) alongside invalidateNamespaceSchema.
    Regression tests: out-of-band rewrite (RED-proven pre-fix), in-process
    declare, empty-cache heal, failure-not-cached.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
